# Line endings must never be rewritten in this repository.
#
# The README publishes MD5 checksums for raw.csv and analysis.csv, and the
# whole point of the repo is that a stranger can verify them. Git's default
# on Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes every one of
# those hashes: raw.csv becomes 4c0038e9f569bfe6e199116f6469732d instead of
# 7b68a001709821c71ece5b8ed209d4d3. A reader following the instructions would
# get a mismatch and reasonably conclude the data had been altered.
#
# -text disables all conversion, so the bytes on disk are the bytes committed.

raw.csv        -text
analysis.csv   -text
*.csv          -text
*.svg          -text

# Scripts and prose keep LF everywhere, so run_all.sh works under bash on any
# platform. A CRLF shell script fails with a confusing "bad interpreter" error.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
